info
# Issue #1933: the batched GraphQL issue-state query (are_issues_open)
# partially failed -- a per-node `Could not resolve` error left some issue
# numbers unresolved, and the parallel per-issue `issue_view` fallback ran
# for exactly those numbers instead of the whole batch. The payload names
# the unresolved numbers (the telemetry the incident lacked).
# Info, not warning (rework review): the edge-trigger dedupe that makes
# this fire once per newly-unresolved number lives on the Issues instance,
# and instance lifetime depends on the caller. The single-repo supervisor
# (supervise.run_supervised) keeps one GitHub for the whole process, so
# there a persistent stale blocker emits one row per process. But the
# fleet supervisor (fleet_loop) builds a fresh GitHub per repo on every
# pass, so there the same blocker emits once per pass per repo -- an
# every-pass warning row into check_warning_events is the flood shape
# #1271/#1768 already burned once for check_warning_events. At info the
# per-pass rows still record the degradation each pass without alarming
# on an expected repeat.
